## NEW AND URGENT: the default model of two engines is EOL in four weeks

The homepage price list now marks:

- **`llama3-chat-8b` ("Llama 3.1 8B") — EOL 30.09.26**
- **`llama3-chat-70b` ("Llama 3.3 70B") — EOL 30.09.26**
- `kimi-k2.7-code-1100b` — **EOL 11.09.26** (ten days)

`llama3-chat-8b` is `Engine::AKIOpenAI::default_model` AND `Engine::AKIAnthropic::default_model`;
`Engine::AKI::default_model` is `llama3_8b_chat`, the native-endpoint name of the same model. Per
AKI's own documented behaviour ("Requests to unknown model names will fall back onto the Minimax
M2.5 model"), after 2026-09-30 every Langertha AKI engine used with its default model will
**silently answer from MiniMax M2.5 instead** — no error, no warning, a different model, a
different context window (65536 -> 196680) and a different price. This is exactly the trap
CLAUDE.md already warns about ("check `$response->model` if it matters which model replied"),
except it will fire on the default path.

Recommendation: pick a new default before 2026-09-30. `minimax-m2.5-230b` is the honest choice —
it is what the silent fallback lands on anyway, it is rated Supported for tools, and it is the
model the worker's earlier 2026-08-24 probe used. Ironically it is also **absent from the public
price list** (it appears only as a vendor logo), despite being the documented fallback target.
Worth its own ticket if this one is about to close.

